<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parikshit Narayan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1603–<a href="/years/1613">1613</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parikshit">Parikshit</a> Narayan was the last independent king of Koch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajo">Hajo</a>, the eastern Koch kingdom in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>. The son of Raghudev, he was a rival of his Koch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> cousins, who allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>. Mughal armies, aided by Koch Bihar, defeated him in 1613, and his kingdom was annexed to the Mughal Empire.</p></div>
